# Data And Privacy

- Room is the source of truth. Save note detail and FTS changes transactionally and preserve stable block ordering.
- Never use destructive migration. Export every schema version to `code/app/schemas/` and add migration tests for schema changes.
- Keep UUID string IDs, injected timestamps, soft delete semantics, and FTS indexing of title/Markdown/OCR.
- Store attachment bytes only in app-private storage; Room stores metadata and validated relative paths, never blobs.
- Import through staging plus atomic move, enforce the 50 MB limit, compute checksums, and roll back partial batches.
- Use Photo Picker/SAF and read-only FileProvider grants. Never request broad storage permission.
- Normalize images and remove EXIF/GPS metadata. Validate MIME, headers, paths, IDs, and provider streams.
- Soft delete keeps files; permanent removal deletes unreferenced files only after metadata save succeeds.
- Keep `android:allowBackup="false"` and do not add `INTERNET` permission or network-backed SDKs.
- Scanner, OCR, audio recording, waveform extraction, and playback must remain fully local.
